<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Zeeland</h1><p class="st-meta">1323 CE – 1581 CE (approx.) · capital Middelburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The island county at the mouths of the Scheldt, Maas and Rhine, disputed by Holland and Flanders and later a stronghold of the Dutch Revolt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The islands of Zeeland had long been disputed between the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-flanders">Flanders</a> and the counts of Holland, who shared them in a complex arrangement. By the Treaty of Paris in 1323 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> gave up its claims, and Zeeland became a county ruled by the counts of Holland, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middelburg">Middelburg</a> as its main town.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Zeeland was a land of reclaimed islands, dykes and seaports. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middelburg">Middelburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zierikzee">Zierikzee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veere">Veere</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Flushing</a> traded in wine, salt, cloth and fish, and the islands were vulnerable to great floods. The county had its own estates but shared rulers with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holland">County of Holland</a>, passing with it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">Wittelsbachs</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/burgundian-state">Burgundian State</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1572 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-beggars">Sea Beggars</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Flushing</a>, and Zeeland became, with Holland, the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. It joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-utrecht">Union of Utrecht</a> in 1579, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration">Act of Abjuration</a> of 1581 it was a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-zeeland.jpg" alt="County of Zeeland" width="320" height="410"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_County_of_Zeeland_(1350).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1323 CE – 1581 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Middelburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William III of Holland, Jacqueline of Bavaria, Philip the Good</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zeeland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1452&amp;focus=county-of-zeeland" aria-label="County of Zeeland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4762 395 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Zeeland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5082 651L5097 634M5082 651L5118 774M5082 651L5102 664M5082 651L5099 670M5082 651L5097 634"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5097 634h0M5118 774h0M5102 664h0M5099 670h0M5097 634h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5082 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5082 651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Middelburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1452&amp;focus=county-of-zeeland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
